":null,"delta15n":null,"infinite":false,"percentc":null,"percentn":null,"labnumber":"Poz-30105","reservoir":null,"geochronid":54688,"geochronage":11220,"geochrontype":"Carbon-14","geochronnotes":null,"percentcollagen":null,"radiocarbonmethod":"accelerator mass spectrometry","geochronerrorolder":60,"geochronerroryounger":60,"geochronmaterialdated":"Polytrichum leaf fragments bark"},"thickness":1,"agelimitolder":11280,"chroncontrolid":134325,"agelimityounger":11160,"chroncontrolage":11220,"chroncontroltype":"Radiocarbon"}]}}],"defaultchronology":43946},"sitedescription":"Small oval lake. Physiography: small cirque glacier that drained into Lusvatnet during the\r\nLateglacial. Surrounding vegetation: Open birch woodland dominated by Betula pubescens ssp. tortuosa and with a predominantly ericaceous or tall-fern-dominated understory clothes the steep lower slopes. Above the tree-line, the vegetation is composed of ericaceous dwarf-shrubs and grasses on sheltered slopes, open grass-heath on exposed ridges, and cliff vegetation around the head of the lake where several arctic-alpine and montane species occur."}}],"message":"Retrieved all tables"}